1. Create a Constructor To create an object.

// POJO Class
// EmployeeVo.java

// Constructor // Constructor Name Should be same as the ClassName
public EmployeeVo(int empId,String empName,int empAge,String branch,int empSalary,String bank){

	this.empId = empId;
	this.empName = empName;
	this.empAge = empAge;
	this.branch = branch;
	this.empSalary = empSalary;
	this.bank = bank;

}
// Constructor

// object

EmployeeVo empVo = new EmployeeVo();

// object


//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

2. Generally for Objects Default value is NULL.

eg:
private static Main instance; // will have an NULL value as default.

/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

3. 

i. For Variable Declaration we will say -> intializing a value.
ii. for Object Declaration we will say -> instantiating

